ns a controlled pirouette on one foot into an arabesque, arms extended, the floating towers sliding past behind her. Her expression shifts from tension to a confident small smile.  [16–20s] Extreme low worm's-eye angle. She performs a final front tuck flip, lands cleanly with both feet on the line, knees absorbing, arms opening wide. The camera pulls back and rises to a wide shot; she holds the final pose, chin lifted, looking toward the distant clouds.  Physics: every jump shows push-off, hand or foot contact on the line, and balance recovery. The line sags slightly under her weight and rebounds. Hair and fabric follow her motion and the wind. Danger is felt through wobbles and the drop below, but she never falls.  Audio: high-altitude wind, fabric flapping <whoosh>, soft line creak <creak> on landings, a faint shimmer <ting> at the glint. No music, no dialogue, no subtitles, no text.

